  a kind row whole (judges_appointed): {'en': "the judges appointed — 'and Moses chose men of valor from all Israel and set them heads over the people, rulers of thousands ...' (18:25); the hard matter to Moses (18:26)", 'he': 'וַיִּבְחַר מֹשֶׁה אַנְשֵׁי חַיִל מִכָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וַיִּתֵּן אֹתָם רָאשִׁים עַל הָעָם (and Moses chose men of valor from all Israel and set them heads over the people, rulers of thousands ... — Exod 18:25)', 'form': 'act', 'witness': ['Exod 18:25 | ויבחר משה אנשי חיל מכל ישראל ויתן אתם ראשים על העם', 'Exod 18:26 | את הדבר הקשה יביאון אל משה'], 'ink': 'Exod 18:25-26; Exod 18:21', 'corpus': 'exo_18_jethro_and_the_judges (STEP_Ex_18_25); exo_18_jethro_and_the_judges (STEP_Ex_18_26)', 'tape': 'submitted by cold_run_exodus_story.py [subjects: moses]; re-submitted on the sequential tape by cold_run_sequence.py; consumed by law_exodus_story (cold_run_exodus_story.py) -> courts_established, hard_cases_to_moses', 'fields': ['over', 'denominations']}
  a kind row whole (spies_commanded): {'en': "the spies commanded — 'send for yourself men that they may spy out the land of Canaan which I give to the children of Israel; one man, one man for his fathers' tribe you shall send, every one a prince among them' (Num 13:2) — Reish Lakish: 'for yourself', at your discretion (Sotah 34b:3); Deut 1:22-23 the people's asking; the spy-verb the ark's of 10:33", 'he': "שְׁלַח לְךָ אֲנָשִׁים וְיָתֻרוּ אֶת אֶרֶץ כְּנַעַן אֲשֶׁר אֲנִי נֹתֵן לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אִישׁ אֶחָד אִישׁ אֶחָד לְמַטֵּה אֲבֹתָיו תִּשְׁלָחוּ כֹּל נָשִׂיא בָהֶֽם (send for yourself men that they may spy out the land of Canaan which I give to the children of Israel; one man, one man for his fathers' tribe you shall send, every one a prince among them — Num 13:2)", 'form': 'speech', 'witness': ['Num 13:2 | שלח לך אנשים ויתרו את ארץ כנען אשר אני נתן לבני ישראל איש אחד איש אחד למטה אבתיו תשלחו כל נשיא בהם'], 'ink': 'Num 13:1-2; Onkelos Num 13:1-2; Deut 1:22-23; Sotah 34b:3', 'corpus': 'num_13_spies_sent (STEP_Nm_13_1, STEP_Nm_13_2; claim SH13A-01)', 'tape': "submitted by cold_run_shelach.py [subjects: moses] (the narrative scene, THE NUMBERS WALK 4b); re-submitted on the sequential tape by cold_run_sequence.py; consume
  a kind row whole (decree_declared): {'en': "the decree declared — 'say to them: as I live, says the LORD, surely as you have spoken in My ears, so I will do to you: in this wilderness your carcasses shall fall, and all your counted by all your number, from twenty years old and upward, who have murmured against Me; surely you shall not come into the land... save Caleb son of Jephunneh and Joshua son of Nun; but your little ones... I will bring in... and your sons shall be shepherds in the wilderness forty years... by the number of the days you spied out the land, forty days, a day for a year, a day for a year, you shall bear your iniquities forty years' (Num 14:26-35) — the census set (Bamidbar's engine CALLED), a day for a year (Ezek 4:6 verbatim), forty against Deut 2:14's thirty-eight", 'he': 'אֱמֹר אֲלֵהֶם חַי אָנִי נְאֻם יְהוָה אִם לֹא כַּאֲשֶׁר דִּבַּרְתֶּם בְּאָזְנָי כֵּן אֶֽעֱשֶׂה לָכֶֽם (say to them: as I live, says the LORD, surely as you have spoken in My ears, so I will do to you — Num 14:28) · בַּמִּדְבָּר הַזֶּה יִפְּלוּ פִגְרֵיכֶם וְכָל פְּקֻדֵיכֶם לְכָל מִסְפַּרְכֶם מִבֶּן עֶשְׂרִים שָׁנָה וָמָעְלָה אֲשֶׁר הֲלִֽינֹתֶם עָלָֽי (in this wilderness your carcasses shall fall, and all your counted by all you
  a kind row whole (pardoned_and_decreed): {'en': "pardoned, and the decree's rider — 'and the LORD said: I have pardoned according to your word; but as I live, and all the earth shall be filled with the glory of the LORD: all the men who have seen My glory and My signs... and have tried Me these ten times... shall not see the land which I swore to their fathers; but My servant Caleb, because another spirit was with him and he followed Me fully, him I will bring into the land where he went, and his seed shall possess it; and the Amalekite and the Canaanite dwell in the valley: tomorrow turn and journey into the wilderness by the way of the Red Sea' (Num 14:20-25) — 'I have pardoned' once in the Bible; Caleb's entitlement paid at Josh 14:13-14; the turn back's run at Num 21:4", 'he': 'וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה סָלַחְתִּי כִּדְבָרֶֽךָ (and the LORD said: I have pardoned according to your word — Num 14:20) · וְעַבְדִּי כָלֵב עֵקֶב הָֽיְתָה רוּחַ אַחֶרֶת עִמּוֹ וַיְמַלֵּא אַחֲרָי וַהֲבִֽיאֹתִיו אֶל הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר בָּא שָׁמָּה וְזַרְעוֹ יוֹרִשֶֽׁנָּה (but My servant Caleb, because another spirit was with him and he followed Me fully, him I will bring into the land where he went, and his seed shall possess it — Num 14:24) · וְהָֽעֲמָלֵקִי
  a kind row whole (smitten_to_hormah): {'en': "smitten to Hormah — 'and the Amalekite and the Canaanite who dwelt in that mountain came down and smote them and beat them down to Hormah' (Num 14:45) — the name used six chapters before its naming at 21:3 (THE PROLEPTIC NAME); Deut 1:44 'as bees do'; Judg 1:17 the second naming", 'he': 'וַיֵּרֶד הָעֲמָלֵקִי וְהַֽכְּנַעֲנִי הַיֹּשֵׁב בָּהָר הַהוּא וַיַּכּוּם וַֽיַּכְּתוּם עַד הַֽחָרְמָֽה (and the Amalekite and the Canaanite who dwelt in that mountain came down and smote them and beat them down to Hormah — Num 14:45)', 'form': 'act', 'witness': ['Num 14:45 | וירד העמלקי והכנעני הישב בהר ההוא ויכום ויכתום עד החרמה'], 'ink': 'Num 14:45; Onkelos Num 14:45; Deut 1:44; Num 21:3; Judg 1:17', 'corpus': 'num_14_rejection (STEP_Nm_14_45; claim SH14A-10)', 'tape': 'submitted by cold_run_shelach.py [subjects: israel] (the narrative scene, THE NUMBERS WALK 4b); re-submitted on the sequential tape by cold_run_sequence.py; consumed by law_shelach (cold_run_shelach.py) -> defeated (the status — smitten and beaten down to Hormah by Amalek and the Canaanite)', 'fields': ['by', 'to']}
  a kind row whole (edom_refused): {'en': "Edom refused — 'and Edom said to him: you shall not pass through me, lest I come out against you with the sword' (Num 20:18) — Esau's blessing 'by your sword you shall live' (Gen 27:40) at its run; Onkelos 'those who kill'", 'he': 'וַיֹּאמֶר אֵלָיו אֱדוֹם לֹא תַעֲבֹר בִּי פֶּן בַּחֶרֶב אֵצֵא לִקְרָאתֶֽךָ (and Edom said to him: you shall not pass through me, lest I come out against you with the sword — Num 20:18)', 'form': 'speech', 'witness': ['Num 20:18 | ויאמר אליו אדום לא תעבר בי פן בחרב אצא לקראתך'], 'ink': 'Num 20:18; Onkelos Num 20:18; Gen 27:40', 'corpus': 'num_20_meribah_edom_aaron (STEP_Nm_20_1 through STEP_Nm_20_29; claims CH20A-01 through CH20A-10)', 'tape': "submitted by cold_run_chukat.py [subjects: edom] (the narrative scene, THE NUMBERS WALK 6b); re-submitted on the sequential tape by cold_run_sequence.py; consumed by law_chukat (cold_run_chukat.py) -> refused (the STATUS on Edom — 'you shall not pass through me')", 'fields': ['words']}
  a kind row whole (edom_came_out_against): {'en': "Edom came out against them — 'and he said: you shall not pass; and Edom came out against him with much people and with a strong hand; and Edom refused to let Israel pass through his border, and Israel turned away from him' (Num 20:20-21) — 'with a strong hand' the Exodus' phrase turned; 'refused' Jacob's verb; Deut 2:4-8, 2:28-29 the other arm (the passage bought)", 'he': 'וַיֹּאמֶר לֹא תַעֲבֹר וַיֵּצֵא אֱדוֹם לִקְרָאתוֹ בְּעַם כָּבֵד וּבְיָד חֲזָקָֽה (and he said: you shall not pass; and Edom came out against him with much people and with a strong hand — Num 20:20) · וַיְמָאֵן אֱדוֹם נְתֹן אֶת יִשְׂרָאֵל עֲבֹר בִּגְבֻלוֹ וַיֵּט יִשְׂרָאֵל מֵעָלָֽיו (the verse continues — Num 20:21)', 'form': 'act', 'witness': ['Num 20:20 | ויאמר לא תעבר ויצא אדום לקראתו בעם כבד וביד חזקה', 'Num 20:21 | וימאן אדום נתן את ישראל עבר בגבלו ויט ישראל מעליו'], 'ink': 'Num 20:20-21; Onkelos Num 20:20-21; Exod 6:1; Gen 37:35; Deut 2:4-8, 2:28-29', 'corpus': 'num_20_meribah_edom_aaron (STEP_Nm_20_1 through STEP_Nm_20_29; claims CH20A-01 through CH20A-10)', 'tape': 'submitted by cold_run_chukat.py [subjects: edom] (the narrative scene, THE NUMBERS WALK 6b); re-submitted on the sequential tape by col
