  an effect row whole (plea_made): {'en': "a plea made — the STATUS a spoken request writes on the one asked, with no close of its own: Moses to Hobab, 'come with us and we will do you good... leave us not, I pray' (Num 10:29-32) — Hobab's refusal ('I will not go') and Moses' second asking recorded as the value; the answer is not in the ink (Judg 1:16, 4:11 the readback)", 'he': 'וַיֹּאמֶר אַל נָא תַּעֲזֹב אֹתָנוּ (and he said: leave us not, I pray — Num 10:31)', 'ledger_op': 'status', 'ink': 'Num 10:29-32; Onkelos; Sifrei Bamidbar 78:1-81:1', 'corpus': 'num_10_trumpets_depart (STEP_Nm_10_29 through STEP_Nm_10_32; claim BH10A-07)', 'exam': 'law_beha (cold_run_beha.py) on hobab_asked — the status on hobab'}
  an effect row whole (oath_sworn): {'en': "an oath sworn — the STATUS the swearing writes on the swearer at the stretch's seats: Esau to Jacob 'swear to me as of this day; and he swore to him' (25:33), Isaac and Abimelech 'and they swore each to his brother' (26:31), Jacob 'by the Fear of his father Isaac' (31:53); Bereshit Rabbah 63:14 (the oath on the sale: still feared — the frozen unit's read); 31:53 the oath's grade sacred or profane (the unit's read)", 'he': 'הִשָּׁבְעָה לִּי כַּיּוֹם וַיִּשָּׁבַע לוֹ (swear to me as of this day, and he swore to him — Gen 25:33)', 'ledger_op': 'status', 'ink': "Gen 25:33, 26:31, 31:53, 24:3 and 24:9 (the family engine's sworn_by_the_name — the oath by the Name is its own effect), 22:16 (God's — sworn_by_himself); Bereshit Rabbah 63:14, 74:15; (O8 S4, 2026-09-08) Gen 47:31 ('swear to me, and he swore to him' — Joseph to Jacob) and 50:25 (the sons of Israel to Joseph) written by law_joseph", 'corpus': 'gen_43_isaac_twins_birthright (STEP_Gn_25_33); gen_45_wells_covenant_esau_wives (STEP_Gn_26_31); gen_54_pursuit_heap_two_tongues (STEP_Gn_31_53)', 'exam': 'cold_run_mamre.py (twins; wells; heap)'}
