  the rows for joshua / caleb / edom / moab / the-court / sihon / og / the-sons-of-gad: [{'id': 'yehoshua', 'en': 'Joshua (Exod 17:9)', 'kind': 'person', 'members': [{'token': 'yehoshua', 'units': ['exo_17_massah_and_amalek']}, {'token': 'joshua', 'units': ['step9-scenes']}], 'note': "The successor's DEBUT — unintroduced, unpatronymed, no office: commissioned mid-battle-order (17:9) and first narrated doing exactly as told (17:10 — the full obedience-formula). The write-command is set in HIS ears (17:14: the erasure-notice briefed to the man who will fight Amalek's remnant). Exod 24:13 (the minister on the mountain), 33:11 (the tent), Num 13:16 (the name expanded), Deut 31 (the charge) armed.\n"}, {'id': 'moab', 'en': 'Moab, son of the firstborn daughter, father of the Moabites (Gen 19:37)', 'kind': 'person', 'members': [{'token': 'moab', 'units': ['step9-scenes']}]}, {'id': 'the_court', 'en': "the court — the judges appointed over the people who judged at all times (Exod 18:25-26), the deputies' docket (24:14), the majority's rule (23:2); its docket carries custody when a case is held until it be declared", 'kind': 'institution', 'members': [{'token': 'the-court', 'units': ['step9-scenes']}]}, {'id': 'caleb', 'en': "Caleb son of Jephunneh — the spy of Judah (Num 13:6; the hushing 13:30; the plea with Joshua 14:6-9; 'another spirit' and the entitlement 14:24; lived 14:38; 26:65; 32:12; Deut 1:36); Josh 14:6-14 the payment — Hebron, forty and forty-five years, eighty-five, Moses' oath 'that day' the ink of Numbers never wrote; Judg 1:12-20; Sotah 34b:7 at the graves of the forefathers (Rava); 1 Chr 2:18 son of Hezron (Sotah 11b:23 'son of Jephunneh' as turning away)", 'kind': 'person', 'members': [{'token': 'caleb', 'units': ['step9-scenes']}]}, {'id': 'edom', 'en': "Edom the nation — Esau's descendants at Seir, 'your brother Israel' (Num 20:14): the king of Edom refused the passage twice, 'you shall not pass through me, lest I come out against you with the sword' (20:18, 20:20 — with much people and a strong hand), 'and Israel turned away from him' (20:21); Deut 2:4-8, 2:28-29 the other arm (the passage bought — the row edom_passage); Deut 23:8 'you shall not abhor an Edomite, for he is your brother'; the person Esau and Gen 36's kings (the_kings_of_edom) are other rows", 'kind': 'people', 'members': [{'token': 'edom', 'units': ['step9-scenes']}]}, {'id': 'sihon', 'en': "Sihon king of the Amorite at Heshbon — refused Israel's passage, went out to Jahaz and was smitten with the edge of the sword, his land possessed from Arnon to Jabbok (Num 21:21-31); his earlier war on Moab's former king (21:26 — Chullin 60b: Ammon and Moab purified through him); Deut 1:4, 2:24-37 (the hardening), 3:2, 29:6, 31:4; Josh 12:2; Judg 11:19-22; Ps 135:11, 136:19; Niddah 61a: Og's brother", 'kind': 'person', 'members': [{'token': 'sihon', 'units': ['step9-scenes']}]}, {'id': 'og', 'en': "Og king of Bashan — came out to Edrei, 'do not fear him' said to Moses, smitten with his sons and people until no survivor, his land possessed (Num 21:33-35); Deut 3:1-11 the retelling with the pronouns shifted and his iron bed nine by four cubits (3:11 — [9, 4] by the parser); 32:33; Josh 12:4, 13:12; Berakhot 54b the mountain; Niddah 24b, 61a of the Rephaim, Sihon's brother; Zevachim 113b of the flood's generation (the row og_lore)", 'kind': 'person', 'members': [{'token': 'og', 'units': ['step9-scenes']}]}, {'id': 'the_sons_of_gad', 'en': "the sons of Gad — the tribe as one grantee of the land east (Num 32:33 'to the sons of Gad'), the builders of Dibon, Ataroth, Aroer, Atroth-shophan, Jazer, Jogbehah, Beth-nimrah and Beth-haran (32:34-36 — 'fortified cities and folds for sheep'); 'Dibon Gad' the itinerary's witness (33:45-46); Joshua 13:24-28 the allotment retold ('the border of the sons of Gad'), 22:1-9 the release; Deuteronomy 33:20-21 Gad's blessing ('the lawgiver's portion'); the registry's gad is Jacob's son (Genesis 30:11), the compound party the_sons_of_gad_and_reuben the stipulation's", 'kind': 'collective', 'members': [{'token': 'the-sons-of-gad', 'units': ['step9-scenes']}]}]
  the registry rows' shape (the last row): {'id': 'nobah', 'en': "Nobah — 'and Nobah went and took Kenath and its daughters, and called it Nobah after his own name' (Num 32:42): his one seat as a person; Kenath's other seat 1 Chronicles 2:23 ('Geshur and Aram took Havvoth-jair from them, with Kenath and its daughters'); THE HOMOGRAPH TRAP: Nobah the place on Gideon's route against Midian, 'east of Nobah and Jogbehah' (Judges 8:11 — the two names' only other seat, Jogbehah Gad's city of 32:35)", 'kind': 'person', 'members': [{'token': 'nobah', 'units': ['step9-scenes']}]}
